  "visualDNA": {
    "Overview": "Typical settings are dim ancestral halls, desolate mortuary houses, walled courtyard mansions, rural Lingnan villages, and dark night forests, all tied to Chinese ghost and funeral lore. Key recurring items are yellow Taoist fulu, glutinous rice, peachwood swords, copper coins, and eight-trigram mirrors, all taken from real Taoist exorcism traditions. The genre’s most iconic figure is the jiangshi, a reanimated corpse in a formal Qing Dynasty mandarin robe with pale, green-tinged skin, rigid outstretched arms, and a fixed hopping movement caused by stiff limbs."
  },
